---
---

<section
  id="about"
  class="about relative z-10 overflow-hidden border-t border-[color-mix(in_srgb,var(--color-accent)_8%,var(--color-border))] bg-canvas"
  aria-labelledby="about-heading"
>
  <div class="about-glow about-glow--teal" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="about-glow about-glow--violet" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="about-grid relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8" data-reveal>
    <div>
      <p class="mono about-eyebrow">Why I build this</p>
      <h2 id="about-heading" class="font-display about-quote">
        <span class="about-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</span>I started building{' '}
        <span class="text-brand-gradient">the tools I wished had existed.</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="about-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="about-text">
      <p class="about-lead">
        After years working across financial services, aviation, telecom, and healthcare, I kept running into the same
        structural problems: security added at the end, findings without context, tools that generated noise instead of
        clarity, and teams with no practical path to improve.
      </p>
      <p>
        Not platforms designed for enterprise sales cycles, but practical, open-source tooling built for teams that
        actually need to ship secure software without a dedicated security department for every service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each project here came from a real problem I encountered or observed directly. The goal is always the same:{' '}
        <strong>reduce friction, increase visibility, and make security something teams want to integrate, not avoid.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .about-glow {
    position: absolute;
    border-radius: 50%;
    filter: blur(70px);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .about-glow--teal {
    width: 420px;
    height: 420px;
    left: -140px;
    top: -160px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 16%, transparent);
  }

  .about-glow--violet {
    width: 380px;
    height: 380px;
    right: -120px;
    bottom: -180px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent-2) 18%, transparent);
  }

  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .about-eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .about-quote {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .about-mark {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.6em;
    line-height: 0.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.15em;
    color: var(--color-accent-2);
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .about-rule {
    width: 4.5rem;
    height: 2px;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-accent), var(--color-accent-2));
  }

  .about-text {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-left: clamp(0rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .about-text p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 52ch;
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 85%, var(--color-muted));
  }

  .about-text .about-lead {
    font-size: 17.5px;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .about-text strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .about-text {
      padding-left: 0;
      border-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
